    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "## Summary\n\nTreesitter highlighting for **svelte files that contain a `<script>` block** breaks in Neovim 0.12.x (and current nightly): the highlighting renders for the first pass, then the extmarks are cleared and never re-set, leaving the buffer without any treesitter highlighting. Svelte files *without* a script block highlight fine, and other languages (html, lua, ts, etc.) are unaffected.\n\n## Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Neovim 0.12.4 (or nightly), with the svelte parser + queries installed (e.g. via nvim-treesitter `main` branch + `tree-sitter-cli`).\n2. Enable native highlighting, e.g.:\n   ```lua\n   vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd(\"FileType\", {\n     pattern = { \"svelte\" },\n     callback = function(ev) pcall(vim.treesitter.start, ev.buf) end,\n   })\n   ```\n3. Open this file in the TUI:\n   ```svelte\n   <script lang=\"ts\">\n     let count: number = 0;\n   </script>\n   <div class=\"a\">\n     <button onclick={increment}>click</button>\n   </div>\n   ```\n\n**Actual:** highlighting appears during the first redraw, then disappears and stays gone (verified by rendering the screen and by dumping the `nvim.treesitter.highlighter` namespace: ~61 ephemeral extmarks are set once, then cleared and never re-set). `vim.treesitter.highlighter.active[buf]` stays non-nil and `parsing=false`, but after the first pass every highlight state ends with `next_row = math.huge` (exhausted iterator) and zero marks.\n\n**Expected:** highlighting persists.\n\n## Additional observations\n\n- Svelte files **without** a script block highlight correctly, so the trigger is the script **injection**.\n- `<script>` with plain javascript (`<script> ... </script>`) is also affected — not just `lang=\"ts\"`.\n- With `vim.g._ts_force_sync_parsing = true` set before opening the buffer, highlighting works correctly (HTML + injected script) and survives edits/redraws. This is the same workaround confirmed by several users for the related injection/async-parsing family of bugs.\n- The svelte injections query produces **two** injected child trees for `<script lang=\"ts\">` (both `typescript` and the catch-all `javascript` from `(svelte_raw_text)`); one child's `included_ranges(true)` is degenerate (e.g. `{6,9,125,6,14,130}` for an 8-line file). Removing the catch-all `javascript` injection pattern did **not** fix the bug, so it is not simply the overlapping injections.\n- The bug persists on `NVIM v0.13.0-dev-1328` (nightly, 2026-08-16), so it is not fixed by anything merged since 0.12.4.\n\n## Environment\n\n- NVIM v0.12.4 (Linux x86_64, CachyOS), also reproduced on `NVIM v0.13.0-dev-1328+g2edb1c0009`\n- Parsers compiled with tree-sitter-cli 0.26.12, installed to `~/.local/share/nvim/site/parser/` (ABI 15)\n- Queries from nvim-treesitter `main` branch (svelte highlights/injections)\n\n## Related\n\n- #32660 — \"Syntax highlight flicker when same buffer open in multiple windows at different scroll positions\" (same async-parsing/injection state-machine family; the merged fix #36503 did **not** fix this case)\n- #33139 — duplicate of the above\n- #35993 — 100% CPU / slow parser with scheduled events (referenced by #36503)\n\n---\n*This issue report was written by an AI assistant (DeepSeek) on behalf of a user who reproduced and debugged the problem.*\n",
