            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Thanks for the responses. I verified it is reproducible **without the nvim-treesitter plugin at all** — pure built-in only:\n\n```\nnvim -u NONE \\\n  -c \"set runtimepath+=<data>/site\" \\      # only for parser + query files\n  -c \"filetype on|set termguicolors\" \\\n  -c \"edit t.svelte|lua vim.treesitter.start(1)\"\n```\n\n(Single `-c` chunks because 0.12 limits the number of `-c` args.) With `<script lang=\"ts\">` + html in the file, the highlighter ends up in this state after the first redraw pass:\n\n```\nhl=true marks=0\nstates=3\nnext_row=inf   # all three highlight states (svelte + injected typescript + injected javascript)\nnext_row=inf\nnext_row=inf\n```\n\ni.e. the decoration-provider pass exhausts every state's iterator (`next_row = math.huge`) and no ephemeral extmarks are (re)set. The final rendered frame has zero treesitter colors. No plugin config is involved — the nvim-treesitter plugin only supplied the parser `.so` + query files on the runtimepath; the processing is entirely `vim/treesitter/highlighter.lua` / `languagetree.lua` (core).\n\nAdditional data points:\n- Trigger is the **script injection**: the same svelte file without a `<script>` block highlights fine; `<script>` with plain javascript (no `lang`) also breaks.\n- `vim.g._ts_force_sync_parsing = true` (core knob) makes it work — survives edits/redraws.\n- Reproduces on `NVIM v0.13.0-dev-1328+g2edb1c0009` (nightly 2026-08-16), which already includes #41090 (idempotent `TSHighlighter.new`), so the double-`start()` orphaned-instance issue is not the cause here.\n- Re: the `pcall` question — the pure repro above calls `vim.treesitter.start(1)` directly without `pcall`, same result. The `pcall` in the issue's example is only to skip filetypes whose parser isn't installed.\n\nInstalled parsers/queries for the repro: svelte (with its `ecma`/`html_tags`/`jsx` query deps), html, typescript, javascript, css-less (no `<style>` used). Parsers compiled with tree-sitter-cli 0.26.12 into `<data>/site/parser` (ABI 15).\n\nHappy to add a minimal `--clean`-style repro or test any candidate fix.\n",
